-- Q278: Risk Assessment [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under AU-C 200.A42, the audit risk model (Audit Risk = Inherent Risk x Control Risk x Detection Risk) requires that when both inherent risk and control risk are assessed as high, detection risk must be set low to maintain audit risk at an acceptably low level. This means the auditor must perform more persuasive, extensive, and timely audit procedures.
Wrong (A): Setting detection risk high when the risk of material misstatement is high would result in unacceptably high overall audit risk.
Wrong (C): Detection risk is not set equal to inherent risk; it is determined as the inverse complement needed to keep audit risk acceptably low.
Wrong (D): A moderate detection risk is insufficient to compensate when both inherent and control risk are high.$EXPL$
